{
  "name": "rename-swc-via-remove-create-and-reference-updates",
  "description": "The identity case: there is no `rename` operation. Renaming `ExampleSWC` to `SpeedSensorSWC` is a `remove`, a `create` and explicit operations for each referring element, all in one change set, so every element the rename touches appears in the reviewed delta instead of being cascaded into on the client's behalf. Since contract `4.0.0` the root composition is one of those referring elements: its member instantiates the component type, and a member naming a type the model no longer declares is `rule:composition.member-unknown-type`.",
  "kind": "example",
  "context": {
    "summary": "The `examples/basic` model. `swcraft impact ExampleSWC` reports two referrers: the connector `Example_to_Consumer`, whose `from.swc` names it, and — since contract `4.0.0` — the root composition `Root`, whose member of that name instantiates it. The requirement `REQ_EXAMPLE_001` is no referrer since contract `11.0.0`: the component names it in its own `satisfies`, so the link travels inside the component's `create` payload and no requirement moves. No task and no sequence maps a runnable of this component.",
    "existing_elements": [
      {
        "layer": "swc",
        "element": "ExampleSWC"
      },
      {
        "layer": "connectors",
        "element": "Example_to_Consumer"
      },
      {
        "layer": "requirements",
        "element": "REQ_EXAMPLE_001"
      },
      {
        "layer": "compositions",
        "element": "Root"
      }
    ],
    "baseline_state": "current",
    "authorization": {
      "approved_scope": [
        {
          "operation": "remove",
          "address": {
            "layer": "swc",
            "element": "ExampleSWC"
          }
        },
        {
          "operation": "create",
          "address": {
            "layer": "swc",
            "element": "SpeedSensorSWC"
          }
        },
        {
          "operation": "update",
          "address": {
            "layer": "connectors",
            "element": "Example_to_Consumer",
            "path": [
              {
                "field": "from"
              },
              {
                "field": "swc"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "operation": "remove",
          "address": {
            "layer": "compositions",
            "element": "Root",
            "path": [
              {
                "field": "members"
              },
              {
                "member": "ExampleSWC"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "operation": "create",
          "address": {
            "layer": "compositions",
            "element": "Root",
            "path": [
              {
                "field": "members"
              },
              {
                "member": "SpeedSensorSWC"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "notes": "The scope names the two referring elements explicitly. A dedicated `rename` would have had to edit them without ever naming them, which is the reason the operation was rejected. The requirement the component satisfies is not among them: since contract `11.0.0` the link lives in the component (`satisfies`), so it is carried by the component's own `create` payload and the requirement file does not change. The composition member takes two entries because a member is identified by its own `name`, and this rename renames the member as well as retargeting it, so the pair is a removal and an addition rather than an `update` of `type`."
    }
  },
